# The DB-bundled OCI client's AUTH Phase 2 (sqlplus 23.26, from
# gvenzl/oracle-free:23-slim, against a disposable test container and a
# throwaway API key), captured whole at gateLogonAlterSession. This is the TTC
# body: what follows the two data-flag bytes.
#
# Its AUTH_ALTER_SESSION is 489 bytes, past the 252-byte CLR short form, and
# the wide long form frames it as
#
#   e9 01 00 00   valLen, ub4 LE
#   fe            long-form marker
#   e9 01 00 00   chunk length, ub4 LE (not a compressed int, not one byte)
#   <489 bytes>
#   00 00 00 00   terminating zero-length chunk, ub4 LE
#   00 00 00 00   flag
#
# Reading the chunk lengths as compressed ints (the thin UseBigClrChunks form)
# refused every sqlplus login with "truncated value" (fclairamb/dbbat#500).

